  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN246.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">tōḻi talaimakaṟku vāyiṉmaṟuttatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">How the confidante refused the door to HIM.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN246.1">
        <l>piṇarmōṭṭu nantiṉ pēḻvā yēṟṟai</l>
        <l>katiraḷak kāral kaḷva ṉāka</l>
        <l><supplied>neṭu</supplied>nīrp poykait tuṇaiyoṭu puṇaru</l>
        <l>malinī rakalvayal <supplied>yā</supplied>ṇa rūra</l>
        <l>pōtār <supplied>kūnta ṉa</supplied>lla vaḷoṭu</l>
        <l>tātār kāñcit taṇpoḻi lakalyā</l>
        <l>ṟāṭiṉai yeṉpa neru<supplied>nai</supplied> yalarē</l>
        <l>kāyciṉa moympiṟ perumpeyark karikā</l>
        <l>lārkali naṟaviṉ veṇṇi vāyi<supplied>ṟ</supplied></l>
        <l>cīrkeḻu <supplied>ma</supplied>ṉṉar maṟaliya ñāṭpi</l>
        <l>ṉimiḻicai muracam porukaḷat toḻiyap</l>
        <l>parikaḷuṇ vēḷi<supplied>ro</supplied>ṭu vēntar cāya</l>
        <l>moyvali yaṟutta ñāṉṟē</l>
        <l>toyyā vaḻuttū rārppiṉum peritē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="4">O man from a fertile village with wide fields [and] ample water,</l>
        <l corresp="1">where a large-mouthed male of the snail with a rough belly</l>
        <l corresp="3">unites with [its] mate in a pond with wide waters,</l>
        <l corresp="2">while the Āral fish, [its] measure an ear [of paddy], becomes a robber,</l>
        <l corresp="5">with a good girl, [her] tresses full of buds,</l>
        <l corresp="7a">you played</l>
        <l corresp="6">in the wide river by the cool grove of Portia trees full of pollen,</l>
        <l rend="indent2" corresp="7b-d">they say, yesterday. [That] gossip,</l>
        <l corresp="14">it is louder than the uproar in imperishable Aḻuttūr</l>
        <l corresp="13">at the time when [its] encompassing strength was cut off</l>
        <l corresp="12">so that kings died along with the toddy-drinking Vēḷirs [and] their horses,</l>
        <l corresp="11">while the drum with a thrumming sound stayed behind on the battle field</l>
        <l corresp="10">in the battle where excellent kings gave fight</l>
        <l corresp="9">at the entrance of Veṇṇi, with toddy [and] a roaring bustle,</l>
        <l corresp="8">[belonging to] Karikāl with a great name for strength [and] burning anger.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

